<title>ITALY: Banco Napoli sells bad debts.</title>
<headline>Banco Napoli sells bad debts.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Struggling southern Italian bank Banco di Napoli said it was selling 12.364 trillion lire worth of shares, stakes and bad debts to its Societa per la Gestione di Attivita (SGA) unit, which manages its bad loans.</p>
<p>Banco di Napoli said in a statement its board had decided the sale of some of its activities within the framework of a restructuring and privatisation programme.</p>
</text>
